<h1>Coast Company Research Summary</h1>
<h2>Company Overview</h2>
<p><strong>Company Name:</strong> Coast<br><strong>Website:</strong> https://www.trycoast.com/<br><strong>Founded:</strong> 2022<br><strong>Location:</strong> New York, NY<br><strong>Status:</strong> Active</p>
<h2>Business Model &amp; Core Product</h2>
<p>Coast is a venture-backed startup that operates as &quot;The API Go-to-Market Platform&quot; - the first AI-powered demo platform specifically designed for API-first companies. The company transforms how technical products are sold, marketed, and implemented by converting API documentation into interactive, bespoke product demos.</p>
<h3>Key Value Proposition</h3>
<ul>
<li>Eliminates the need for prospects to wade through pages of documentation</li>
<li>Removes the burden of building demos from scratch for GTM teams</li>
<li>Enables instant, customized demonstrations of API capabilities for specific prospects</li>
<li>Accelerates commercialization of APIs and enables digital transformation for enterprises</li>
</ul>
<h2>Leadership Team</h2>
<p><strong>Co-Founders:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Spencer Levitt</strong> - Co-founder and CEO</li>
<li><strong>Austin Pager</strong> - Co-founder</li>
</ul>
<p>Both founders are alumni of Y Combinator&#39;s Summer 2021 batch.</p>
<h2>Funding &amp; Financial Performance</h2>
<h3>Funding History</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Total Funding:</strong> $2.1 million in venture funding (as of April 2023)</li>
<li><strong>Funding Status:</strong> Venture-backed startup</li>
<li><strong>Y Combinator:</strong> Summer 2021 batch participant</li>
</ul>
<h3>Financial Metrics (2024)</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Annual Revenue:</strong> $1.7 million</li>
<li><strong>Team Size:</strong> 11-25 employees (sources vary)</li>
<li><strong>Growth:</strong> Bootstrapped growth model after initial funding</li>
</ul>
<h2>Target Market &amp; Customers</h2>
<h3>Primary Market</h3>
<ul>
<li>API-first companies</li>
<li>SaaS businesses with technical products</li>
<li>Enterprise clients requiring secure, scalable demo infrastructure</li>
</ul>
<h3>Use Cases</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Sales Teams:</strong> Purpose-built demos for prospect meetings</li>
<li><strong>Solutions Teams:</strong> Technical implementation demonstrations</li>
<li><strong>Marketing Teams:</strong> Product showcasing and lead generation</li>
<li><strong>Enterprise Clients:</strong> Secure, regulated environment demonstrations</li>
</ul>
<h2>Product Features &amp; Capabilities</h2>
<h3>Core Platform Features</h3>
<ul>
<li>AI-powered demo generation from API documentation</li>
<li>Interactive product demonstrations</li>
<li>Customizable demos for specific prospects</li>
<li>Enterprise-grade security and scalability</li>
<li>Visual platform making APIs more accessible</li>
</ul>
<h3>Enterprise Offering</h3>
<ul>
<li>Secure, scalable demo infrastructure</li>
<li>Compliance with enterprise security requirements</li>
<li>Internal enablement tools</li>
<li>Trusted by regulated enterprises</li>
</ul>
<h2>Market Position &amp; Competitive Advantage</h2>
<h3>Unique Positioning</h3>
<ul>
<li>First-mover advantage in AI-powered API demo space</li>
<li>Focus specifically on API-first companies (niche specialization)</li>
<li>Y Combinator pedigree and network</li>
<li>Strong technical foundation with visual accessibility</li>
</ul>
<h3>Recent Developments</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>2024:</strong> Company underwent a rebranding with new visual identity and website</li>
<li>Positioned as &quot;an operating system for building, selling and scaling APIs&quot;</li>
<li>Emphasis on bold vision and future-focused growth</li>
</ul>
<h2>Company Culture &amp; Vision</h2>
<h3>Mission</h3>
<p>Making APIs more accessible and accelerating commercialization for high-impact digital transformation at the world&#39;s largest enterprises.</p>
<h3>Team Philosophy</h3>
<p>&quot;Meet the team behind the demos—helping every company deliver the right product story, every time.&quot;</p>
<h2>Growth Trajectory</h2>
<h3>Key Milestones</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>2021:</strong> Founded and joined Y Combinator Summer batch</li>
<li><strong>2022:</strong> Official company launch</li>
<li><strong>2023:</strong> Secured $2.1M in venture funding</li>
<li><strong>2024:</strong> Reached $1.7M annual revenue with lean 11-person team</li>
<li><strong>2024:</strong> Completed major rebranding initiative</li>
</ul>
<h3>Current Status</h3>
<ul>
<li>Active and growing company</li>
<li>Hiring across multiple technical and business roles</li>
<li>Expanding enterprise client base</li>
<li>Continuing product development and market expansion</li>
</ul>
<h2>Industry Context</h2>
<p>Coast operates in the intersection of several growing markets:</p>
<ul>
<li>API economy and API-first business models</li>
<li>Sales enablement and demo automation</li>
<li>AI-powered business tools</li>
<li>Enterprise software solutions</li>
</ul>
<p>The company addresses a specific pain point in the API economy where technical products struggle with effective demonstration and sales processes, positioning itself as a critical infrastructure component for API-first businesses.</p>
<hr>
<p><em>Research compiled from: TechCrunch, Y Combinator, LinkedIn, company website, and industry sources</em><br><em>Date: September 18, 2025</em></p>
